+# Task 3 report — bounded source checkpoint complete
+
+Read Task 3 brief/Global Constraints, Task 2 report/review, actual-child candidate/advisory evidence and parent §§4.3–4.5/canonical row contract. Applied clean-code and verification-before-completion to isolated observational helpers. Root alone made SEC requests; this agent made no network/SEC/Azure requests, no commits/staging, and preserved original package deletions, plans and roadmap. Task 3 produces source observations and future decode-probe inputs, not a production parser or Stage 1 readiness approval.
+
+## Matrix and novelty disposition
+
+Ten receipts SEC-0141–0150 cover 2010Q1, 2015Q1, latest closed 2026Q3, open 2026Q4, root ZIP relationship, daily 2026-09-30/2026-10-01 transition and handoff, published 2026-10-02 and daily year transition 2025-12-31/2026-01-02. All URLs were actual retained children. `specimens/matrix.json` links each role, listing receipt, original/derivative hashes, rows and filing-date bounds. Required daily boundaries were present; no absence/substitution or additional sampling was needed.
+
+Five quarterly ZIPs have exactly one DEFLATE `master.idx`, strict ASCII/CRLF, five pipe fields and dashed-accession `.txt` paths. Full streaming reads validate CRC and exact expanded size under 512 MiB before retaining separately hashed derivatives. Isolated temporary extraction directories are removed. Root/open originals and derivatives compare exactly equal at receipt time; future equality is unproven.
+
+First daily SEC-0146 exposed a distinct selected text family: `File Name` header, compact YYYYMMDD dates and LF endings. The strict unknown-header guard exited 1; original bytes, initial command/output and bounded novelty observations remain retained. Root paused requests and obtained owner acceptance “Accept bounded daily-family continuation”, retained in `daily-family-continuation-acceptance.json` at 2026-10-06T00:00:39.782687Z. Only then was the helper explicitly extended and the retained body scanned completely. Daily success commands use distinct `dailyfamilyinspection*` sidecars. The four accepted remaining URLs required four requests and showed no further family/path novelty. Root closed access at 00:06:34.377545Z: 150 attempts, 15,293,779 entity bytes, ten specimen receipts and no access-denial halt. No further SEC access is authorized by this task.
+
+Every row in all retained bodies was inspected; all daily rows are ASCII/LF/five-field compact-date with the same dashed-accession path family. No invalid date or non-extractable path appeared. Nullable accession remains required for unexamined families. Optional `.sit/.z/.Z/.gz` and daily archive alternatives stay unselected/unexamined/unsupported. No unexamined family gains support by analogy; later production golden parser verification remains required.
+
+Daily filing dates may precede the source filename by months and cross quarters/years: 2026-09-30 spans 2025-08-25–2026-09-30; handoff spans 2026-08-12–2026-10-01; published 2026-10-02 spans 2026-03-31–2026-10-02; year-before spans 2025-05-28–2025-12-31; year-after spans 2025-08-27–2026-01-02. Exact raw compact values and minimum/maximum representative rows remain in inspection JSON. Parent valid filing date determines output quarter; preserve all observations and apply existing precedence/approved-withdrawal rules to each affected quarter. No filename-date equality test or deletion from open-snapshot absence is invented. Open-quarter header October 3 does not extend row coverage past October 2.
+
+## Raw contract and bounded space
+
+Original ZIPs remain `<sha256>.zip`; plain daily originals `<sha256>.idx`; decoded ZIP members remain separate `<sha256>.decoded.idx`. Acquisition bodies also remain intact. Root/QTR equality produces shared hash-named files with distinct receipts. Parent `master.idx` is an example; this local evidence naming does not revise a durable production contract. Receipt metadata retains original extension/format/URL, identity content-encoding interpretation, MIME/validators/status/User-Agent/UTC receipt/actual bytes and Content-Length comparison.
+
+68-quarter volume totals exclude root duplication and keep optional representations separate: ZIP 209,670 KB; IDX 1,519,859 KB; gzip 219,223 KB; uppercase Z 393,903 KB; sit 117,188 KB (19 children); lowercase z 55,053 KB (9 children). All labels are KB and none is absent; label rounding/scaling remains unverified. Assuming 1024-based KB gives ZIP planning total 214,702,080 bytes, not exact received bytes. Largest listed ZIP is 2024Q1 4,114 KB; largest retained is 2015Q1 3,901,000 exact bytes with 28,748,322 expanded bytes. Ratios per archive and full terms are in `volume-assessment.json`.
+
+Measured unique originals total 13,425,383 bytes and derivatives 84,787,910 bytes. The one-source model is measured original+expanded lengths plus one largest expanded-size output scratch assumption, twice that generation scratch assumption, and 1 GiB installer/runtime/log reserve: 1,192,636,112 bytes. Co-resident retained-matrix illustration totals 1,258,200,083 bytes. Previously retained Microsoft documentation maps over 1 vCPU to 8 GiB ephemeral capacity, so candidate 2 vCPU maps to that documented capacity. This local planning comparison is not measured processing scratch, all-source expansion tail bound, 4 GiB-memory/3,600-second-runtime fit or integrated Azure behavior. No setting revision is inferred. Stage 7 retains actual fit authority. Recommend bounded one-source investigation units and existing 512 MiB expansion guard; do not design the worker here.
+
+## Annotation defect and recovery
+
+The annotation helper initially used quarterly columns against daily's distinct schema and wrote directly to the CSV. It raised `DictWriter` ValueError after 2,172 daily rows, omitting four tail rows. Diagnosis used the actual headers and immutable SEC-0138/0139 children; exactly four original tail rows were recovered offline. The fix selects daily outcome plus explicit inspection columns and writes a temporary file before atomic replacement. No source refetch occurred.
+
+The first synthetic regression fixture was outside the SEC-* glob; first red/attempted green both failed at the expected-outcome assertion. Their stdout/stderr files were overwritten when correcting the fixture; exact first-fixture output bytes are not separately retained. `annotation-repair-sequence.json` explicitly records this evidence loss and known exit 1; no recreated bytes are presented as original evidence. The corrected `--reproduce-old` algorithm reconstruction exits 1 with the actual schema ValueError. Actual fixed code then exits 0. Current red/green outputs and command receipts preserve that relevant reproduction. An early combined-shell overall exit must not be read as each individual command succeeding.
+
+Full comparison to frozen `.sdd/.../task-2-review.diff` verifies all 372 quarterly and 2,176 daily rows in original order and every original field unchanged except authorized selected statuses/reasons; all four recovered rows match the frozen originals. Daily handoff relations are preserved. New evidence columns are populated only for selected daily bodies.
+
+## Fresh verification and registers
+
+Final commands, start/end UTC, exit codes and full stdout/stderr are in `specimens/*-command.json` and matching output files:
+
+- `check_source_evidence.py 10`: exit 0. Ten receipts, 13 distinct original/derivative files; independent direct `shasum -a 256`, immutable receipt equality, archive member/CRC/content, expanded lengths, complete row/date extrema, selected annotations and direct root/QTR bytes.
+- `check_matrix_preservation.py`: exit 0. Frozen original-field preservation and recovered tail rows confirmed.
+- `check_specimen_offline.py`: exit 0. Synthetic traversal/absolute/extra member/expansion/strict decoding rejection; no live or golden-parser claims.
+- `check_annotation_offline.py`: exit 0 after corrected pre-fix reproduction exit 1.
+- `python3 -m py_compile` on all seven Task 3 investigation tools: exit 0.
+
+With exclusive root coordination, updated selected quarterly/daily annotations and appended Task 3 evidence/discrepancy records without replacing prior rows. Root retains access-window accounting. Source-assessment documents measured/assumed space and unsupported tails. D-14 historical middle-quarter coverage remains open; Task 4 handles isolated runtime/import/decode probes, while production parser verification belongs to later stages. Root review and Stage 1 readiness remain outstanding.
+
+Across all listed alternatives, the largest labeled body is 2026Q1 `master.idx`, 32,282 KB. It is unselected/unfetched; its label is not an expanded-byte measurement. The largest retained expansion remains 28,748,322 bytes, reinforcing that the sample maximum is not a full-range bound.
